# Allowlist, not a denylist.
#
# The previous version restated .gitignore's artefact list by hand, which drifts
# the moment .gitignore gains an entry — the same duplication the Makefile's
# `clean` target was fixed to stop doing. It also used bare `__pycache__` and
# `*.pyc`, which are PATH-ANCHORED in .dockerignore and so matched only the
# context root: src/<pkg>/__pycache__/ was being sent in the context and baked
# into the image by `COPY src ./src`.
#
# Inverting removes both problems. This list mirrors the Dockerfile's COPY lines
# exactly, so anything new is excluded by default and adding a COPY means adding
# one line here — a change you cannot forget, because the build fails without it.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!src
!README.md

# Re-excluded inside the allowed paths: nothing gitignored should ride along
# inside src/. These need ** because .dockerignore patterns are path-anchored.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.env
